---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { generateBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';

const title = 'How We Choose Hotels: Selection Methodology & Editorial Standards (2026)';
const description = 'Our public editorial methodology for evaluating hotels in Gurugram. How we evaluate published specifications, verify transit times, examine public review benchmarks, and enforce non-commercial independence.';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Selection Methodology', href: '/how-we-choose-hotels/' }
];

const breadcrumbSchema = generateBreadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Selection Methodology', url: '/how-we-choose-hotels/' },
]);
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/how-we-choose-hotels/"
  jsonLd={breadcrumbSchema}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

  <article class="methodology-page container section-padding">
    <header class="methodology-masthead">
      <div class="masthead-kicker-wrap">
        <span class="editorial-kicker">Editorial Standards & Due Diligence</span>
        <span class="badge badge-brass">Framework</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="methodology-h1 font-serif">How We Choose & Evaluate Hotels in Gurugram</h1>
      <p class="lead methodology-lead">
        In an accommodation market overwhelmed by sponsored search placements and manipulated guest reviews, our directory operates under a strict, non-commercial editorial standard. Here is exactly how properties are selected, researched, and maintained.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="methodology-layout-grid">
      <!-- Main Content Column -->
      <div class="methodology-main-content">
        <section class="editorial-article-block">
          <h2 class="font-serif">1. The Definition of "Best" & "Top"</h2>
          <div class="article-prose">
            <p>
              We do not believe any single hotel is objectively the "best" for all people. Gurugram accommodates vastly different traveler cohorts: a corporate executive negotiating an M&A transaction in DLF Cyber City requires completely different amenities than a solo software auditor visiting Golf Course Road on a strict per diem, or a family seeking open resort lawns near the Aravallis.
            </p>
            <p>
              When we designate a property as "best for" a specific purpose (e.g., "Best for Large-Scale Conventions" or "Best for Rapid Metro Walkability"), that characterization must be defended by verifiable physical specifications, corroborated operational history, and observable geographic advantages.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="editorial-article-block">
          <h2 class="font-serif">2. The Five Objective Selection Pillars</h2>
          <div class="selection-pillars-flow">
            <div class="selection-pillar-card card">
              <div class="pillar-serial font-serif">01</div>
              <div class="pillar-details">
                <h3 class="font-serif">Verifiable Physical Facilities</h3>
                <p>Every listed facility (dedicated in-room desks, soundproof double-glazing, power backup generators, meeting room capacities, and swimming pools) is corroborated against official corporate architectural documentation and active municipal registrations.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="selection-pillar-card card">
              <div class="pillar-serial font-serif">02</div>
              <div class="pillar-details">
                <h3 class="font-serif">Transit Reality & U-Turn Verification</h3>
                <p>We reject radial "as-the-crow-flies" distance measurements. Gurugram’s highway infrastructure (NH-48, Shankar Chowk, IFFCO Chowk) requires significant U-turns. We record real driving minutes and verify walkability to Delhi Metro Yellow Line or Gurugram Rapid Metro stations.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="selection-pillar-card card">
              <div class="pillar-serial font-serif">03</div>
              <div class="pillar-details">
                <h3 class="font-serif">Corroborated Public Reputation</h3>
                <p>We cross-reference public sentiment across Google Maps and independent travel forums to understand operational consistency. We explicitly look for recurring patterns: reports of air-conditioning failures during hot summer months, unpaved or flooded approach roads, or noisy banquet disruptions.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="selection-pillar-card card">
              <div class="pillar-serial font-serif">04</div>
              <div class="pillar-details">
                <h3 class="font-serif">Balanced Editorial Reporting</h3>
                <p>No property is flawless. Every hotel profile in our directory features both "Key Strengths" and "Things to Keep in Mind." We transparently highlight highway noise, valet bottlenecks during wedding seasons, compact room footprints, or remote locations.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="selection-pillar-card card">
              <div class="pillar-serial font-serif">05</div>
              <div class="pillar-details">
                <h3 class="font-serif">Non-Commercial Directory (Zero Sponsored Rankings)</h3>
                <p>Hoteliers, management agencies, and hospitality chains cannot purchase inclusion, premium placement, or positive editorial copy. The directory is maintained as an independent, non-commercial public research resource.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="editorial-article-block">
          <h2 class="font-serif">3. Methodology Limitations</h2>
          <div class="limitations-callout card">
            <h3 class="font-serif">What This Directory Can & Cannot Do</h3>
            <ul class="limitations-list" role="list">
              <li>
                <strong>Dynamic Pricing:</strong> Room tariffs in the National Capital Region fluctuate based on corporate demand, wedding dates, and season. All rates displayed are historical starting benchmarks recorded on specific verification dates. Travelers must check official booking channels for live quotes.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>No Pretend First-Hand Stays:</strong> We do not fabricate overnight reviews or pretend to have slept in every room. Our profiles are compiled from published corporate architectural specifications, official reservation portals, public review benchmarks, and verified transit measurements.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="editorial-article-block">
          <h2 class="font-serif">4. Ongoing Freshness & Corrections Pathway</h2>
          <div class="article-prose">
            <p>
              Hotels frequently renovate facilities, change restaurant concepts, or alter shuttle services. We periodically verify contact details, operational status, and transit conditions.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="corrections-action-card card">
            <h3 class="font-serif">Notice a Factual Discrepancy?</h3>
            <p>If you represent a hotel or recently stayed at a property and observed changes in amenities, pricing, or transit access, please let us know immediately.</p>
            <a href="/corrections/" class="btn btn-navy btn-sm">Submit a Correction Request &rarr;</a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: Standards Sidebar -->
      <aside class="methodology-sidebar" aria-label="Editorial policies navigation">
        <div class="sidebar-policy-card card">
          <h3 class="policy-card-title">Trust & Policies</h3>
          <ul class="policy-links-list" role="list">
            <li><a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy & Disclosures</a></li>
            <li><a href="/about/">About This Directory</a></li>
            <li><a href="/corrections/">Submit Corrections</a></li>
            <li><a href="/contact/">Contact Our Desk</a></li>
            <li><a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .methodology-masthead {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto 3.5rem;
  }

  .masthead-kicker-wrap {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .methodology-h1 {
    font-size: 2.35rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--navy-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .methodology-h1 {
      font-size: 3.25rem;
    }
  }

  .methodology-lead {
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 780px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  .methodology-layout-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 3.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .methodology-layout-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 300px;
    }
  }

  .editorial-article-block {
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .editorial-article-block h2 {
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    color: var(--navy-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .article-prose p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    max-width: var(--prose-max);
  }

  .selection-pillars-flow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .selection-pillar-card {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    background-color: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .pillar-serial {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    line-height: 1;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--navy-primary);
    background-color: var(--navy-subtle);
    padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .pillar-details h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--navy-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .pillar-details p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .limitations-callout {
    padding: 2rem;
    background-color: var(--bg-card);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--brass-accent);
  }

  .limitations-callout h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--navy-primary);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .limitations-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .limitations-list li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .limitations-list li::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--brass-accent);
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .limitations-list strong {
    color: var(--navy-primary);
  }

  .corrections-action-card {
    padding: 2rem;
    background-color: var(--forest-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--forest-border);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .corrections-action-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--forest-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .corrections-action-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .sidebar-policy-card {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    position: sticky;
    top: 5.5rem;
    background-color: var(--bg-card);
  }

  .policy-card-title {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .policy-links-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .policy-links-list a {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    transition: color var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .policy-links-list a:hover {
    color: var(--forest-primary);
  }
</style>
